From 7af375e585641d2d10311d49965f3fbc47885eb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:27:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/43] usb_webcam: offer the sizes the camera reports

Applications had to guess which sizes a camera supports. The
producer now publishes the camera's sizes as a B_RESOLUTION
parameter, each item labelled with its frame rate, for example
"1280 x 720 (30 fps)". Setting the parameter chooses the size for
the next connection that does not ask for one; the value is checked
against the camera's list, and a running stream is left alone.
Connect() refuses sizes above 8192 pixels a side, so that the size
of a buffer cannot overflow.

CamDevice gets CountVideoSizes() and VideoSizeAt(); UVCCamDevice
answers them from its frame descriptors. The packing of a size into
the parameter value, the label and the size limit live in
CamVideoSize.h and are covered by CamVideoSizeTest.

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit f1cc4c42fcb9657a6070ecdd3aae5e1bd500f019)
